Z||000000||JohnnyK||09-04-2000||03:18 PM||||I think I found the clutch line (hard to tell that from the rear brake line). Is that the one that starts off with like, braided kevlar or something, then looks like a brake line, then goes back to the braided stuff. Anyways, if that is it, it KIND of looks like there is a small leak. The metal line there looks wet (doesn't feel wet), and right underneath it, the paint is bubbled and disintigrated like it came in contact with brake fluid. Now my question is, it held fluid for about a hundred miles, and I couldn't tell a difference in the fluid level, so would a leak this small have an affect on my clutch not really disengaging at all? (The car does roll, not move, with the clutch pushed in, but I can't really move the shifter without he-man-like strength.) Thanks||||reg||1
